    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter August 9th with a high-ceiling core anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), who draws the premium matchup of the day against Dobnak. With a +14% dynamic platoon boost and a favorable wind-out condition, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our top priority as we hunt for that scarce stolen base production. **Trea Turner** (77.93) and **Kyle Schwarber** (77.21) also project as elite starts against Bieber; both benefit from a +19% SP skill boost and favorable lineup positioning, with **Kyle Schwarber** specifically surging into a top-tier play due to his lead-off role. **Yordan Alvarez** (68.54) remains a must-start despite the absence of an opposing pitcher, as his elite 0.471 xwOBA provides an insulated floor even on rest days for others.\n\nOur lineup construction favors aggressive matchups today, leading to the exclusion of **Josh Smith** (33.53). While **Josh Smith** was the closest to cracking the roster, he was ultimately pushed below the Zebras' 40.0 floor due to a daunting matchup against Luzardo and an unfavorable #8 spot in the lineup. Conversely, **Junior Caminero** (62.17) secures a strong start against the hittable Emerson Hancock. We are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Dillon Dingler**, **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Yordan Alvarez**; should any of these players slide down in the order or be rested, we have depth ready to pivot. Note that **Dillon Dingler** is currently facing the steepest uphill battle with a -15% dynamic platoon penalty against Logan Webb, making his inclusion a test of our depth at the catcher position.",
